{{Quote|I've heard the temple outpost is only defended by a single Jedi, and she's some old lady, so...|Krix Kamerat|<ref name="HRA 8" />}}
The '''Jedi Temple''',<ref name="HRA 8" /> also known as the '''Takodana Outpost Temple''',<ref name="Sav">{{SWYouTube|series=Characters of Star Wars: The High Republic|text=Sav Malagan|video=pGUb41t6LqI}}</ref> the '''Takodana Jedi Temple''',<ref name="Lonely Traveler">{{StoryCite|story=The Lonely Traveler is Home|book=The High Republic: Tales of Light and Life}}</ref> or the '''Takodana Temple''', was a [[Jedi temple]]<ref name="THRA 8">[[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 8|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 8]]</ref> and [[Jedi outpost|outpost]] of the [[Jedi Order]] on [[Takodana]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. The temple was built on [[Nymeve Lake]],<ref name="HRA 8" /> and was headed by [[Jedi Master]] [[Kaktorf]] until he decided to take a temporary leave of absence from the role<ref name="THRA 8" /> in [[382 BBY]].<ref name="Date 2">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[The High Republic Adventures (2022) 8|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2022) 8]] to [[382 BBY]].</ref>

By [[231 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> the [[Kyuzo]] [[Jedi]] Master [[Savina Besatrix Malagán|Sav Malagán]],<ref name="HRA 8" /> who had previously been Kaktorf's [[Padawan]],<ref name="THRA 8" /> came to oversee the temple. The Padawans of the [[Star Hopper]] visited the temple and it was the site of a skirmish with the [[Nihil]] in the time following the [[Valo Republic Fair|Republic Fair]] on [[Valo]], resulting in the destruction of the temple.<ref name="HRA 9">[[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 9|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 9]]</ref><ref name="HRA 10">[[The High Republic Adventures (2021) 10|''The High Republic Adventures'' (2021) 10]]</ref>

